# Loaded only by `vite build --mode android` (web/package.json's
# build:android script) — never by the default `npm run build` used for the
# browser/PWA production deploy (web/railway.json), which reads
# .env.production / platform env vars instead and is untouched by this file.
#
# Capacitor's WebView runs at its own local origin, not the page's real
# host, so api.ts's "same host as the page" fallback (see resolveApiUrl in
# web/src/lib/api.ts) doesn't apply here the way it does for the browser —
# this must be set explicitly to the real production API.
VITE_API_URL=https://server-production-a4fb.up.railway.app

# Public half of the production server's VAPID keypair — see
# web/.env.example. Not a secret, but must match whatever VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY
# the deployed server actually uses (server/.env.example), so left blank
# here rather than filled with a placeholder/dev value. Android push itself
# goes through FCM, not Web Push, but keeping this set is what lets
# SettingsScreen's Web Push code path no-op cleanly if ever reached instead
# of throwing on a missing key.
# VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
